title ALES39 — Lotus's session file: a keeper's whole project as one sealed document
prompt Continue the ALES recursion loop Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds and make progress before checking in; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur
think ALES38 lifted the seal into one parser-agnostic primitive precisely to open this rung. The next durable purely-local rung the README and both seal witnesses named is the session file — a keeper saves TWO things (the rack of held audio, ALES33; the cue sheet arrangement map, ALES22) and until now they saved/loaded separately, two files free to drift apart into different takes. A project is one thing; it deserves one document.
think Chose it Lindy-first crux-first. Lindy: the top-level save/load a keeper reaches for every session (open my project, save my project) is the most-read gesture the suite has, and one sealed document carrying the whole project verified is the culmination of the persistence arc. Crux-first: the hard-but-tractable core is EXACT sectioning under one seal — parse_rack and parse_sheet each consume their WHOLE text (confirmed by reading parse_rack: it splits on newline and a non-empty trailing piece after the empty final is BadRecord), so the bundle must hand each parser exactly its own bytes, and the whole must verify before either half is trusted.
think Shape: lotus/session.rye over seal + rack_sheet + cue_sheet (+ parse_int for the manifest). save renders the two sub-records into a bounded scratch (sized max_body = rack_sheet.max_rack_sheet_bytes + cue_sheet.max_sheet_bytes + manifest_max) to learn their exact byte lengths, writes a `format lotus-session-v1` manifest (rack <n> / cue <n>) then the two records verbatim, and seals the whole under a distinct `format lotus-session-sealed-v1` header via seal.begin/finish. load runs seal.open over the ENTIRE body (the whole-project gate), then splits by the manifest: payload after the three manifest lines must measure EXACTLY rack_len + cue_len (its own integrity check) or BadRecord, then parse_rack sees payload[0..rack_len] and parse_sheet sees payload[rack_len..] with the cue's master position-bound passed through after the gate.
think Length-delimited, never delimiter-scanned — a slot or marker name may hold any character (names carry spaces already), so a sentinel line could collide with real content; a byte-length manifest cannot. Strict decimal parse_int (.{}) on each section length refuses a leading zero. SessionError = seal.SealError || rack_sheet.RackSheetError || cue_sheet.MarkerTextError (Zig merges by name so BadRecord/Overflow coincide rather than tripling).
obs GREEN on the first build across six cases: a two-slot rack (real stereo PCM) and a four-marker cue sheet over one 500-sample master round-tripped whole (each slot's audio byte-for-byte by pasting it back, every marker's position and name); a flipped byte in the CUE half AND a separately flipped byte in the RACK half each refused DigestMismatch with both outputs empty (the seal covers the whole body, proven from both ends); a truncated tail refused DigestMismatch; a plain unsealed record and a bare sealed header with no manifest each refused BadRecord; a save into a too-small buffer refused Overflow.
obs Witness tools/ales_session_witness.rish GREEN; tame_style_check GREEN (bans clean); width-check clean. Reused whole: seal.begin/finish/open, rack_sheet.render_rack/parse_rack, cue_sheet.render_sheet/parse_sheet, tally_copy.copy_disjoint (no new @memcpy site), parse_int strict decimal. Purely local — a Sha256 over an in-process text record; no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real meter, no real speaker; every custody gate untouched. With the session file the purely-local persistence arc is whole — file, edit, save, seal, load, merge, rename, and now one document for the whole project verified before trust.
loom witness=ales_session_witness result=green digest=sha256 hex_len=64 build=first cases=6 sections=2 delimit=byte-length reused=seal+rack_sheet+cue_sheet
file lotus/session.rye ALES39 module — save / load bundling the rack and the cue sheet over one master into one sealed document, the whole verified before either half is trusted
file tools/ales_session_witness.rish the witness that builds and proves it GREEN on metal
file active-designing/20260814-155054_fill-ales39-lotus-session.md the self-approved design read for the round
file lotus/README.md front door synced — status list (ALES39 session file), the session.rye rung entry, road-on paragraph, stamp
recommend keep-going ALES40 can carry the persistence arc onward — a session that also holds the master audio itself (not only the rack of spans), or the SIGNED session (who wrote it, via a Kumara key) and the ALES0-wire carry, both module seams for Keaton's word
